From 124edcc3ff6df1804f6461ae8a6e3953d91aade3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yx-lim <87307371+yx-lim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:01:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Grid references: spoken MGRS grids place reports directly;
 every position shows its grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New backend/services/grid.py (from EDTH-FreeTeam backend/grid.py). It converts with the
  mgrs package (matches GeographicLib's GeoConvert on 34/34 test points) and reads grids
  spoken in English, Ukrainian and Russian (60/60 on a held-out phrase set).
- process_transcript: a grid read out on the radio beats any landmark. A grid more than
  GRID_MAX_KM (50 km) from DEMO_CENTER is treated as misheard: it is rejected, the landmark
  route is used, and the reason goes in placement_method.
- Every event gets an `mgrs` field. Its precision follows the uncertainty circle, so a
  ±40 m position shows a 100 m square, never a 10 m one.
- UI: the grid shows in the latest-extraction panel, the event log and the map tooltips.
- backend/tests/test_grid_pipeline.py: offline end-to-end test (fake Gemini and geocoder).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
